 ],
 "section_summary": "This section contains diplomatic despatches, statistical reports, memoranda, and correspondence concerning Japan's wood pulp and paper manufacturing industries during the post-World War II Allied occupation between 1946 and 1948. The primary document is SCAP Natural Resources Section Report No. 56 (September 1946), which comprehensively surveys historical production, raw material consumption, pulping techniques, and mill directories, emphasizing the severe impact of losing pulpwood resources and chemical pulp mills in Karafuto, Korea, and Formosa. Subsequent documents include transmittals of updated 1946–1947 production statistics requested by the U.S. Department of Commerce, an inquiry from the American Paper & Pulp Association, and an internal State Department administrative memorandum.",
