   "start_page": 2,
   "summary": "This report surveys Japan's wood pulp and paper manufacturing industry, detailing historical production trends, raw material consumption, and post-World War II shortages of wood, coal, and chemicals. It analyzes distinct pulping processes—groundwood, sulfite, kraft, soda, and rayon pulp—highlighting the critical loss of major pulpwood sources and chemical pulp mills in Karafuto, Korea, and Formosa. Extensive statistical tables and directories outline rated capacities, machine specifications, and geographic locations of pulp and paper mills across Japan.",
   "title": "Natural Resources Section Report No. 56: The Wood Pulp Industry of Japan",
   "to": "Supreme Commander for the Allied Powers"
  },
